.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MIDNIGHTBSD-SETTINGS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm midnightbsd-settings
.Nd graphical settings for Midnight Workspace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens the GTK 3 Midnight Workspace settings application.
Its Appearance, Desktop and panel, and Session pages edit the user INI file
used by
.Xr midnight-wm 1 .
Click Apply to save changes.
Appearance and desktop changes update a running Midnight Workspace;
session restoration choices take effect at the next login.
The Session page also controls whether Midnight Workspace starts XScreenSaver
at the next login when it is installed.
The editor preserves unknown INI keys and comments.
It reports malformed or externally changed files rather than overwriting them.
The Session page can clear saved folder and application sessions.
The Application defaults page selects installed handlers for web links,
HTML files, email links, calendar, folder, text, image, and PDF files,
and the panel terminal.
These choices are written to the current desktop's user XDG association and
terminal preference files when Apply is clicked.
.Pp
The application-specific option is:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -version
Print the project version and exit without opening a window.
.El
GTK also accepts its standard display and help options.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev DISPLAY , XAUTHORITY
Select and authenticate to the X server.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for
.Pa midnight-wm/config.ini ;
defaults to
.Pa ~/.config .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/midnight-wm/config.ini
User configuration at the default XDG config location.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/midnight-wm/config.ini
Installed example with all supported settings.
.It Pa ~/.config/midnightworkspace-mimeapps.list
Application link and file defaults in Midnight Workspace.
.It Pa ~/.config/midnightworkspace-xdg-terminals.list
Preferred terminal in Midnight Workspace.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr midnight-wm 1 ,
.Xr midnightbsd-search 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt
